{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-108801" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x+y}{x+y+2}.\n$$\n\nUsing a substitution of the form $z=x+y,$ transform the differential equation into an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z).$ What is the function $f(z)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065291/state.json" "file_sha256" "22d30e8798957c821bd5c1f2f8c2bc7a7513bf5ffa02ea34701311b358310b9a"} {"question" "q-108801" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz=x+y.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=1+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-1 & =\\frac{z}{z+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{z}{z+2}+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{2z+2}{z+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(z+1)}{z+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(z)=\\frac{2(z+1)}{z+2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065291/state.json" "file_sha256" "22d30e8798957c821bd5c1f2f8c2bc7a7513bf5ffa02ea34701311b358310b9a"} {"question" "q-108801" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065291/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7c087e16148b5ffdaacf74e040bf8c6fcbd24d886fbb3ef6555b836a4de2707a"} {"question" "q-108801" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065291/state.json" "file_sha256" "22d30e8798957c821bd5c1f2f8c2bc7a7513bf5ffa02ea34701311b358310b9a"} {"question" "q-108801" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{2(z+1)}{z+2}"] ["math" "\\frac{2z+1}{2z}"] ["math" "\\frac{2z+1}{z+2}"] ["math" "\\frac{2z}{z+2}"] ["math" "\\frac{z+1}{2z}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065291/state.json" "file_sha256" "22d30e8798957c821bd5c1f2f8c2bc7a7513bf5ffa02ea34701311b358310b9a"} {"question" "q-108801" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2(z+1)}{z+2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065291/state.json" "file_sha256" "22d30e8798957c821bd5c1f2f8c2bc7a7513bf5ffa02ea34701311b358310b9a"} {"question" "q-108804" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=4-\\sqrt{y-2x+3}.\n$$\n\nUsing a substitution of the form $z=y-2x,$ transform the differential equation into an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z).$ What is the function $f(z)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065291/state.json" "file_sha256" "22d30e8798957c821bd5c1f2f8c2bc7a7513bf5ffa02ea34701311b358310b9a"} {"question" "q-108804" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz=y-2x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+2 & =4-\\sqrt{z+3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=2-\\sqrt{z+3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(z)=2-\\sqrt{z+3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065291/state.json" "file_sha256" "22d30e8798957c821bd5c1f2f8c2bc7a7513bf5ffa02ea34701311b358310b9a"} {"question" "q-108804" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065291/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7c087e16148b5ffdaacf74e040bf8c6fcbd24d886fbb3ef6555b836a4de2707a"} {"question" "q-108804" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065291/state.json" "file_sha256" "22d30e8798957c821bd5c1f2f8c2bc7a7513bf5ffa02ea34701311b358310b9a"} {"question" "q-108804" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\sqrt{z+3}"] ["math" "2-\\sqrt{z+3}"] ["math" "2-\\sqrt{z-3}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{z+3}-2"] ["math" "\\sqrt{z-3}-4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065291/state.json" "file_sha256" "22d30e8798957c821bd5c1f2f8c2bc7a7513bf5ffa02ea34701311b358310b9a"} {"question" "q-108804" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2-\\sqrt{z+3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065291/state.json" "file_sha256" "22d30e8798957c821bd5c1f2f8c2bc7a7513bf5ffa02ea34701311b358310b9a"} {"question" "q-108840" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=(x+y+2)^{3}-1.\n$$\n\n \nThe general solution to this equation can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ng(x,y)=C-2x,\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant. What is $g(x,y)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065291/state.json" "file_sha256" "22d30e8798957c821bd5c1f2f8c2bc7a7513bf5ffa02ea34701311b358310b9a"} {"question" "q-108840" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz=x+y.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=1+\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-1 & =(z+2)^{3}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=(z+2)^{3}.\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is separable. So, we separate the variables and integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{(z+2)^{3}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{(z+2)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2(z+2)^{2}} & =x+K \\\\ \\frac{1}{(z+2)^{2}} & =C-2x,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-2K.$\n\nFinally, we write the equation in terms of $y$ and $x$ using our original substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{(x+y+2)^{2}}=C-2x\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x,y)=\\frac{1}{(x+y+2)^{2}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065291/state.json" "file_sha256" "22d30e8798957c821bd5c1f2f8c2bc7a7513bf5ffa02ea34701311b358310b9a"} {"question" "q-108840" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065291/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7c087e16148b5ffdaacf74e040bf8c6fcbd24d886fbb3ef6555b836a4de2707a"} {"question" "q-108840" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065291/state.json" "file_sha256" "22d30e8798957c821bd5c1f2f8c2bc7a7513bf5ffa02ea34701311b358310b9a"} {"question" "q-108840" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{(x+y)^{4}}"] ["math" "-\\frac{2}{(x+y+2)^{2}}"] ["math" "\\frac{(x+y+2)^{3}}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{(x+y)^{2}}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{(x+y+2)^{2}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065291/state.json" "file_sha256" "22d30e8798957c821bd5c1f2f8c2bc7a7513bf5ffa02ea34701311b358310b9a"} {"question" "q-108840" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{(x+y+2)^{2}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065291/state.json" "file_sha256" "22d30e8798957c821bd5c1f2f8c2bc7a7513bf5ffa02ea34701311b358310b9a"} {"question" "q-108841" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{e}^{x+y}-x-y}{x+y}.\n$$\n\n \nThe general solution to this equation can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ng(x,y)=C-x,\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant. What is $g(x,y)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065291/state.json" "file_sha256" "22d30e8798957c821bd5c1f2f8c2bc7a7513bf5ffa02ea34701311b358310b9a"} {"question" "q-108841" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz=x+y.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=1+\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-1 & =\\frac{{e}^{z}-z}{z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{e}^{z}}{z}.\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is separable. So, we separate the variables and integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{z}{{e}^{z}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\int z{e}^{-z}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing integration by parts on the left side,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=z & \\,⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{-z} & \\,⟹\\,v=-{e}^{-z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int z{e}^{-z}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -z{e}^{-z}+\\int {e}^{-z}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -z{e}^{-z}-{e}^{-z} & =x+C \\\\ -{e}^{-z}(z+1) & =x+K \\\\ {e}^{-z}(z+1) & =C-x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-K.$\n\nFinally, we write the equation in terms of $y$ and $x$ using our original substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n{e}^{-x-y}(x+y+1)=C-x\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x,y)={e}^{-x-y}(x+y+1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065291/state.json" "file_sha256" "22d30e8798957c821bd5c1f2f8c2bc7a7513bf5ffa02ea34701311b358310b9a"} {"question" "q-108841" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065291/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7c087e16148b5ffdaacf74e040bf8c6fcbd24d886fbb3ef6555b836a4de2707a"} {"question" "q-108841" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065291/state.json" "file_sha256" "22d30e8798957c821bd5c1f2f8c2bc7a7513bf5ffa02ea34701311b358310b9a"} {"question" "q-108841" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{e}^{-2x-2y}"] ["math" "{e}^{-x-y}"] ["math" "{e}^{-x-y}(x+y+1)"] ["math" "{e}^{x+y}(1-x-y)"] ["math" "{e}^{x+y}(x+y)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065291/state.json" "file_sha256" "22d30e8798957c821bd5c1f2f8c2bc7a7513bf5ffa02ea34701311b358310b9a"} {"question" "q-108841" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{e}^{-x-y}(x+y+1)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065291/state.json" "file_sha256" "22d30e8798957c821bd5c1f2f8c2bc7a7513bf5ffa02ea34701311b358310b9a"} {"question" "q-149710" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\sqrt[3]{x-2y}.\n$$\n\nUsing a substitution of the form $z=x-2y,$ transform the differential equation into an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z).$ What is the function $f(z)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065291/state.json" "file_sha256" "22d30e8798957c821bd5c1f2f8c2bc7a7513bf5ffa02ea34701311b358310b9a"} {"question" "q-149710" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz=x-2y.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=1-2\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =\\sqrt[3]{z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=1-2\\sqrt[3]{z}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(z)=1-2\\sqrt[3]{z}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065291/state.json" "file_sha256" "22d30e8798957c821bd5c1f2f8c2bc7a7513bf5ffa02ea34701311b358310b9a"} {"question" "q-149710" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065291/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7c087e16148b5ffdaacf74e040bf8c6fcbd24d886fbb3ef6555b836a4de2707a"} {"question" "q-149710" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065291/state.json" "file_sha256" "22d30e8798957c821bd5c1f2f8c2bc7a7513bf5ffa02ea34701311b358310b9a"} {"question" "q-149710" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1-2\\sqrt[3]{z}"] ["math" "2\\sqrt[3]{z-1}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt[3]{z}"] ["math" "\\sqrt[3]{2z-1}"] ["math" "\\sqrt[3]{z}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065291/state.json" "file_sha256" "22d30e8